---
import StudioLayout from '../../../layouts/StudioLayout.astro';
import { studioCapabilities, studioVoiceNotes } from '../../../lib/studioHelp';
---

<StudioLayout
  title="Content help"
  description="Private guide to Studio Content — voice, discrete updates, preview, and publish."
  heading="Content help"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-xl px-4 py-5 md:py-8">
    <p class="text-sm">
      <a href="/studio/help" class="text-gel underline-offset-2 hover:text-gold hover:underline">
        ← All help
      </a>
      {' · '}
      <a href="/studio/content" class="text-gel underline-offset-2 hover:text-gold hover:underline">
        Open Content
      </a>
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
      Site updates live under Content. Speak or type a request, or open a discrete tile. Reference
      device: <span class="text-spotlight">{studioVoiceNotes.referenceDevice}</span>.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">Getting started</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-muted">
        <li>Open <a href="/studio/content" class="text-gel hover:text-gold">Content</a>.</li>
        <li>
          Choose <span class="text-spotlight">Speak or type</span>,{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">Gallery photo</span>,{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">Lesson rates</span>,{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">Performer facts</span>,{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">Reel</span>,{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">Short bio</span>, or{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">Press quote</span>.
        </li>
        <li>
          For voice updates, hold <span class="text-spotlight">Hold to speak</span> (or type). For
          gallery, rates, and facts, edit the fields (and attach a photo for gallery) directly.
        </li>
        <li>
          Tap preview, review (or tweak the fields), then{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">Publish to site</span>.
        </li>
        <li>Wait a few minutes for the site rebuild; Studio shows progress when publishing is allowed.</li>
      </ol>
      <figure class="space-y-3 pt-2">
        <img
          src="/images/studio-help/studio-help-hub.jpg"
          alt="iPhone 17 Safari showing Studio Content with Speak or type and tiles for Gallery photo, Lesson rates, and other updates."
          class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-sm border border-line"
          width="720"
          height="1080"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="text-center text-xs text-muted">
          On Content — pick a job, then edit → preview → publish.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 space-y-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">Discrete tiles</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Discrete tiles skip voice and open a short form. Same Preview and Publish steps as Speak or
        type.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-spotlight">Gallery photo</h3>
        <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-muted">
          <li>Open <span class="text-spotlight">Gallery photo</span> from Content.</li>
          <li>
            Choose a JPEG, PNG, or WebP. Pick tags from the fixed list (custom tags can’t be added) and
            crop focus if you want. Optionally set a gallery file name — Studio explains why it matters
            and adds <span class="text-spotlight">.md</span> if you leave it off.
          </li>
          <li>
            If Studio warns that the photo is already on the site, pick a different file — or confirm
            only if you mean to publish a duplicate.
          </li>
          <li>
            Preview the tile, then publish. New photos appear first in the gallery. Captions stay empty
            on the public gallery.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <figure class="space-y-3">
          <img
            src="/images/studio-help/studio-help-gallery.jpg"
            alt="iPhone 17 Safari showing the Gallery photo editor with a selected headshot, tags, crop focus, and Preview gallery photo."
            class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-sm border border-line"
            width="720"
            height="1080"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-center text-xs text-muted">
            Attach a photo, choose allowlisted tags and focus, then preview the gallery tile.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-spotlight">Lesson rates (and other forms)</h3>
        <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-muted">
          <li>Open <span class="text-spotlight">Lesson rates</span> (or Facts, Reel, Short bio, Press quote).</li>
          <li>Edit the fields shown — rates prefill from the live book page.</li>
          <li>Preview shows a read-only site-style confirmation, then publish.</li>
        </ol>
        <figure class="space-y-3">
          <img
            src="/images/studio-help/studio-help-rates.jpg"
            alt="iPhone 17 Safari showing Lesson rates with 30- and 60-minute dollar fields and Preview rate update."
            class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-sm border border-line"
            width="720"
            height="1080"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-center text-xs text-muted">
            Dollar amounts for 30- and 60-minute sessions — Reset to live restores current prices.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">Voice on iPhone</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Voice is dictation into the Message box — not a separate command list. Speak the same kind of
        request you would type. Steps below are for {studioVoiceNotes.referenceDevice}.
      </p>

      <figure class="space-y-3">
        <img
          src="/images/studio-help/studio-help-hold-to-speak.jpg"
          alt="iPhone 17 Safari showing Studio with a finger holding the Hold to speak button while a booking message appears in the Message field."
          class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-sm border border-line"
          width="720"
          height="1080"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="text-center text-xs text-muted">
          Hold <span class="text-spotlight">Hold to speak</span>, say your update, then release.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-spotlight">Hold to speak</h3>
        <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Open Content in Safari on your iPhone.</li>
          <li>Press and hold <span class="text-spotlight">Hold to speak</span> (do not just tap).</li>
          <li>Keep holding while you talk. The button shows Listening…</li>
          <li>Lift your finger when you finish. Your words fill the Message box.</li>
          <li>Edit by typing if needed, then tap <span class="text-spotlight">Preview update</span>.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>{studioVoiceNotes.replacesNotAppends}</p>
        <p>{studioVoiceNotes.fallback}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-spotlight">Allow the microphone (first time)</h3>
        <figure class="space-y-3">
          <img
            src="/images/studio-help/studio-help-safari-mic.jpg"
            alt="iPhone 17 Safari system alert: elysetindall.com would like to access the microphone, with Don’t Allow and Allow."
            class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-sm border border-line"
            width="720"
            height="1080"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-center text-xs text-muted">
            Tap <span class="text-spotlight">Allow</span> when Safari asks for the microphone.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>The first time you hold <span class="text-spotlight">Hold to speak</span>, Safari asks for microphone access.</li>
          <li>Tap <span class="text-spotlight">Allow</span>.</li>
          <li>
            If you chose Don’t Allow, open the iPhone <span class="text-spotlight">Settings</span> app
            → <span class="text-spotlight">Apps</span> → <span class="text-spotlight">Safari</span> →
            <span class="text-spotlight">Microphone</span> (or Settings → Safari → scroll to
            elysetindall.com under Website Settings) and turn microphone access on, then reload Content.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          If the button reads <span class="text-spotlight">Voice not supported</span> or
          <span class="text-spotlight">Mic unavailable — type instead</span>, use the keyboard — publishing
          still works the same way.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">What you can say</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Speak or type a clear request. Studio maps it to one of these updates. Include names, dates,
        venues, and prices when they matter — it will not invent credits for you.
      </p>

      <ul class="space-y-8">
        {
          studioCapabilities.map((cap) => (
            <li class="border-b border-line pb-8 last:border-0">
              <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-spotlight">{cap.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{cap.summary}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-gel">Lives at {cap.livePath}</p>
              <p class="mt-4 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted">Try saying</p>
              <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2">
                {cap.examplePrompts.map((prompt) => (
                  <li class="rounded-sm border border-line bg-panel/40 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-spotlight">
                    “{prompt}”
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <div class="space-y-2 rounded-sm border border-line bg-panel/40 p-4 text-sm text-muted">
        <p class="font-semibold text-spotlight">Teaching brand reminder</p>
        <p>
          Private lessons are <span class="text-spotlight">voice lessons</span> only — vocal pedagogy,
          vocal health, and CCM. Do not ask Studio to advertise acting lessons, monologue coaching, or
          scene study.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">Preview &amp; publish</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-muted">
        <li>
          <span class="text-spotlight">Preview</span> drafts the change without going live. For gallery,
          rates, reel, bio, quote, and facts, Preview is a{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">read-only site preview</span> — go Back to edit if something looks
          wrong. Speak-or-type drafts for credits and news can still be adjusted in Preview.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-spotlight">Publish to site</span> (production Studio) commits the change.
          The live site updates after the rebuild (usually a few minutes). On staging, the button reads
          <span class="text-spotlight">Publish to staging branch</span> — updates go to a dated branch
          and a pull request. Test with Actions → <span class="text-spotlight">CD: staging</span>; merge
          the PR to promote.
        </li>
        <li>Use <span class="text-spotlight">Start another update</span> when you are ready for the next change.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <figure class="space-y-3">
          <img
            src="/images/studio-help/studio-help-preview.jpg"
            alt="iPhone 17 Safari showing Studio Preview with a gallery tile confirmation and Publish to site."
            class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-sm border border-line"
            width="720"
            height="1080"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-center text-xs text-muted">
            Confirm the Preview, then publish — or go Back to edit.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="space-y-3">
          <img
            src="/images/studio-help/studio-help-done.jpg"
            alt="iPhone 17 Safari showing Studio Done with update accepted, publishing pipeline, and Start another update."
            class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-sm border border-line"
            width="720"
            height="1080"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-center text-xs text-muted">
            After publish, watch the rebuild and open the page when ready.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</StudioLayout>
